# Proposed right multiplication rows in the Hall--Janko corner coordinates

Bit j in row i is the binary coefficient of orbit j in the image of orbit i.
These nine arrays are sums of the retained condensed-word operators, using the
same nine word lists as `Presentation.Words`. They are fixed data, not an
assertion that they act on the literal corner. That connection, their word span,
and their relation checks are separate proof obligations.

Source: the degree-100 ATLAS J2G1-p100B0 carrier and the reproducible scripts
retained with the five-corner discovery. See source/README.md for provenance.
-/

